  \ to force improvements on the n=26 plateau seems like a recipe for frustration. Instead, I must begin by fully grasping the SOTA method, which involves \"intelligent seeding\" and \"stochastic perturbation.\" Only with this complete understanding can I develop any useful hypothesis. After this, I need to explore the n=29 peak in depth, as this represents the most promising opportunity. Based on the capsule list, it seems Capsule 10, \"New Research Arc (n=26): Hexagonal Seeding with Perturbation,\" which should contain the most detailed account of this work. Then, I plan on reading Capsules 9 and 8 to understand the trajectory that led to the SOTA and then capsules 6 and 7 to further analyze the relationship between `n` and `Σr`. Finally, I will synthesize all this into a research hypothesis. \n\nTherefore, I need to proceed with understanding the current SOTA method. \n\n/execute_action{read 10}\n"
