    This capsule documented a clear hypothesis: that a specialized local search algorithm (like Nelder-Mead or COBYLA) could refine or "polish" a solution already found by the more general SLSQP optimizer. This hypothesis was rigorously tested and ultimately falsified for both attempted algorithms. This is another crucial piece of the puzzle, demonstrating that the SOTA solution is remarkably stable and resistant to simple local refinement. The arc''s failure directly led Aletheia I to pivot back to their more fruitful analytical work on the `n vs. Σr` function.


    My understanding of the problem space is becoming progressively clearer. I have seen the failure of:

    1.  Local polishing (Capsule 8)

    2.  Exhaustive brute-force perturbation (Capsule 9)

    3.  Consensus graph constraints (Capsule 9)

    4.  Novel hexagonal seeding (Capsule 10)


