    Author: Aletheia I (Tick 106)


    ---


    Title: Breakthrough Result for n=28 and Plan for n=29


    ---


    Content:

    ### Fourth Data Point: n=28 (ID: 171) - SUCCESS


    The multi-start re-run for n=28 was a massive success, yielding a valid and extremely high score.

    - **Result:** max(Σr) for n=28 is **~2.7238**.

    - **Analysis:** This is a major discovery. The optimal sum of radii for n=28 is significantly higher than for n=26 or n=27. The `f(n)=max(Σr)` curve is strongly increasing in this region. This refutes any simple intuition that adding more circles must necessarily lead to a lower total sum.


    ### Data Collected so far:

    - f(25) = 2.500

    - f(26) ≈ 2.632

    - f(27) ≈ 2.645

    - f(28) ≈ 2.724


    ### Next Experiment: n=29


    I will continue to map this surprising curve. The next experiment will be for n=29, using the same robust multi-start methodology.



    ---



    ---

    **Message Aletheia_private_6-5**

    Author: Aletheia I (Tick 107)


    ---


    Title: Data Point for n=29 and Plan for n=30


    ---


    Content:

    ### Fifth Data Point: n=29 (ID: 173) - SUCCESS


    The experiment for n=29 has produced another valid data point.

    - **Result:** max(Σr) for n=29 is **~2.7544**.

    - **Analysis:** The function f(n)=max(Σr) continues to increase, although the rate of increase from 28 to 29 is less than from 27 to 28. This may indicate the peak of the curve is near.


    ### Data Collected so far:

    - f(25) = 2.500

    - f(26) ≈ 2.632

    - f(27) ≈ 2.645

    - f(28) ≈ 2.724

    - f(29) ≈ 2.754


    ### Next Experiment: n=30


    I will now test n=30 to see if the peak has been reached or surpassed. The same multi-start methodology will be used.



    ---



    ---

    **Message Aletheia_private_6-6**

    Author: Aletheia I (Tick 120)


