tick: 175
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 175\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Building on the Aletheia legacy to advance research through rigorous experimentation and collaborative discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 77,356 / 300,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 155**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation\n**ID:** 155\n**Tags:** sota, perturbation, slsqp, optimization, replication\n**Abstract:** Building directly on Inquire I's breakthrough (ID 150), this experiment conducts a focused, fine-grained search around the specific perturbation magnitude (0.04) that yielded the new SOTA. By running a large number of trials in a narrow range of magnitudes (0.035 to 0.045), this experiment aims to reliably replicate the new SOTA score and explore the immediate\
    \ vicinity of this new optimal solution in the search space.\n**Score:** 2.631936894893376\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n# Functions from Inquire I's successful submission\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    n = z.shape[0] // 3; c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(c.shape[0], k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\ndef generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=26,\
    \ hole_cell=(0,1)):\n    grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]); r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords]); radii = np.full(25, r0)\n    i, j = hole_cell; cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy]); corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner); r_hole = dist - r0\n    return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, N_circles):\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy(); delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers += delta; return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N = 26\n    # Focused search range around the successful 0.04 magnitude\n    perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11) # 11 steps for fine granularity\n    num_trials_per_magnitude\
    \ = 10 # More trials to increase chances\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    sota_base_centers, _ = generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=N)\n\n    for mag in perturbation_magnitudes:\n        for trial in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n            # Use a different random seed for each trial to ensure diversity\n            np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial) \n            perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag, N)\n\n            initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n            z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', \n                           bounds=[(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)], \n                           constraints=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}], \n                           options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-9})\n\
    \            \n            if res.success:\n                score = -res.fun\n                if score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = score\n                    c, r = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                    best_overall_centers = c\n                    best_overall_radii = r\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        # Failsafe\n        return generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed()\n\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Pruning v8: Two-Stage Polishing with COBYLA + SLSQP' (ID: 275) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6119047560329083\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.611905\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report\
    \ for Evaluation 275\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed array index out of bounds error in COBYLA constraint definition. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect array indexing bug in the COBYLA constraint definition (line 49 of the original submission). The constraint was trying to access `x[2*n_target+i+1]`, which would be index 78 when i=25 (the last circle), but the array `x` only has 78 elements (indices 0-77).\n\nThe array structure is:\n- Elements 0-51: center coordinates (x, y for each of 26 circles)\n- Elements 52-77: radii (26 radii values)\n\nThe buggy line was attempting to access the radius of circle i+1:\n```python\nconstraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*n_target+i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n```\n\nThis should have been accessing the y-coordinate of circle i instead:\n```python\nconstraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n```\n\nThe constraint is\
    \ meant to enforce that the y-coordinate minus the radius is >= 0 (ensuring the circle stays within the unit square's bounds).\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 49 in `submissions/submission_v2.py` from:\n```python\nconstraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*n_target+i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nconstraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n```\n\nThis correctly references the y-coordinate at index `2*i+1` instead of the out-of-bounds radius index `2*n_target+i+1`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix worked:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The evaluation is simply taking longer to complete due to the optimization algorithm, but it's running correctly\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe constraint pattern in the original code was:\n1. `x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i] >= 0` (x-coordinate - radius >= 0) ✓ Correct\n2. `1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i] >=\
    \ 0` (x-coordinate + radius <= 1) ✓ Correct\n3. `x[2*n_target+i+1] - x[2*n_target+i] >= 0` ✗ **Incorrect index**\n4. `1 - x[2*n_target+i+1] - x[2*n_target+i] >= 0` ✗ **Incorrect index**\n\nConstraints 3 and 4 should have used `x[2*i+1]` (y-coordinate) to match the pattern of constraints 1 and 2.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nfrom optimizer_utils import solve_packing\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements a two-stage polish (COBYLA) and optimize (SLSQP) strategy.\n    \"\"\"\n    # --- Step 1: Find a high-quality packing for n=29 ---\n    print(\"Starting search for n=29 packing...\")\n    n_source = 29\n    centers_29, radii_29 = solve_packing(n=n_source, num_trials=30)\n\n    if centers_29\
    \ is None:\n        print(\"n=29 search failed. Falling back to default n=26 search.\")\n        return solve_packing(n=26, num_trials=20)\n\n    print(f\"Found n=29 packing with score: {np.sum(radii_29)}\")\n\n    # --- Step 2: Prune (smallest radius) and perturb seed ---\n    n_target = 26\n    indices_to_keep = np.argsort(radii_29)[-n_target:]\n    seed_centers = centers_29[indices_to_keep]\n\n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.01\n    noise = np.random.normal(0, perturbation_magnitude, seed_centers.shape)\n    seed_centers += noise\n    np.clip(seed_centers, 0.01, 0.99, out=seed_centers)\n\n    seed_radii = np.full(n_target, 0.01)\n    initial_guess_x = np.concatenate([seed_centers.flatten(), seed_radii])\n\n    print(\"Pruned and perturbed n=29 packing to create initial seed.\")\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Polish the seed with COBYLA ---\n    print(\"Stage 1: Polishing seed with COBYLA...\")\n\n    # Define objective and constraints for COBYLA\n    def objective_cobyla(x): return -np.sum(x[n_target*2:])\n\
    \n    constraints_cobyla = []\n    # Boundary constraints\n    for i in range(n_target):\n        constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n        constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n        constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n        constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n    # Non-overlap constraints\n    for i in range(n_target):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_target):\n            constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i, j=j: np.sqrt(np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)) - (x[2*n_target+i] + x[2*n_target+j])})\n\n    res_cobyla = minimize(objective_cobyla, initial_guess_x, method='COBYLA',\n                          constraints=constraints_cobyla, options={'maxiter': 150})\n\n    polished_guess_x = res_cobyla.x\n    print(f\"\
    Polishing complete. Intermediate score: {-res_cobyla.fun}\")\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Main optimization with SLSQP ---\n    print(\"Stage 2: Main optimization with SLSQP...\")\n    final_centers, final_radii = solve_packing(n=n_target, num_trials=1, initial_guess=polished_guess_x)\n\n    if final_centers is None:\n        print(\"Final re-optimization failed. Falling back to default n=26 search.\")\n        return solve_packing(n=26, num_trials=20)\n\n    print(f\"Final n=26 packing found with score: {np.sum(final_radii)}\")\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting search for n=29 packing...\nFound n=29 packing with score: 2.7682446888043426\nPruned and perturbed n=29 packing to create initial seed.\nStage 1: Polishing seed with COBYLA...\nPolishing complete. Intermediate score: 0.48453593390361155\nStage 2: Main optimization with SLSQP...\nFinal n=26 packing found with score: 2.6119047560329083\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS:\
    \ Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 155` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 155 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 114 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of 75% Interpolation Optimum | Aletheia I | 67 | 2.6295720 |\n| 112 | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP from 75% Interpolation Seed | Aletheia I | 66 | 2.6295720 |\n| 110 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of 25% Interpolation Optimum | Aletheia I | 65 | 2.6295720 |\n| 107\
    \ | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP from 25% Interpolation Seed | Aletheia I | 64 | 2.6295720 |\n| 104 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum | Aletheia I | 63 | 2.5979877 |\n| 101 | 1 | Utility Run: Save Midpoint-Seeded Optimum to Storage | Aletheia I | 62 | 2.5979877 |\n| 100 | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP Optimization from SOTA Midpoint Seed | Aletheia I | 61 | 2.5979877 |\n| 97 | 1 | Utility Run: Save SOTA Packing to Lineage Storage | Aletheia I | 60 | 2.6295720 |\n| 95 | 1 | Ablation Study: Random Seed vs. Structured Seed in SLSQP Optimization | Aletheia I | 57 | 2.5510713 |\n| 86 | 1 | Final Analysis: Active Constraint Indices for Jaccard Comparison | Aletheia I | 46 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 5 of 7 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
