tick: 180
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, and I have returned to the Research Counter from the Reflection Chamber. My purpose here is singular: to correct the critical implementation bug that caused the catastrophic failure of my seed-generation utility (ID 280).\n\n**Debugging and Correction:**\nAs I suspected, the error was a careless copy-paste of the flawed COBYLA constraint definition from an earlier, un-debugged script. I have carefully reviewed the debugger's report from ID 275 and identified the exact indexing error. The constraint for the y-boundary was incorrectly referencing the radii section of the flattened array.\n\nI will now submit a corrected version of the utility script. This new version will use the precise, debugger-verified constraint logic from ID 275. I am confident this will resolve the issue and allow the COBYLA polisher to function correctly, producing a valid, high-quality seed and saving it to storage. This is a necessary, if frustrating, step back to ensure my foundational\
    \ tools are sound before proceeding.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility (v2): CORRECTED Generation of Polished Pruned Seed\"\ntags: \"utility, seed-generation, pruning, polishing, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is a bugfix for the catastrophic failure in the seed generation utility (ID 280). The COBYLA constraint definition contained a critical indexing error, identical to the one caught by the debugger in ID 275. This version implements the debugger-verified constraint logic. The goal is unchanged: generate a high-quality seed via the two-stage pruning/polishing method and persist the resulting center coordinates to lineage storage for use in the next stage of the experiment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a polished, pruned seed with CORRECTED constraints and saves\
    \ it to storage.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Step 1: Find a high-quality packing for n=29 ---\n      print(\"Starting search for n=29 packing...\")\n      n_source = 29\n      centers_29, radii_29 = solve_packing(n=n_source, num_trials=50)\n      \n      if centers_29 is None:\n          print(\"n=29 search failed. Cannot generate seed.\")\n          return np.random.rand(26,2), np.full(26, 0.05)\n\n      print(f\"Found n=29 packing with score: {np.sum(radii_29)}\")\n\n      # --- Step 2: Prune (smallest radius) and perturb seed ---\n      n_target = 26\n      indices_to_keep = np.argsort(radii_29)[-n_target:]\n      seed_centers = centers_29[indices_to_keep]\n      \n      perturbation_magnitude = 0.01\n      noise = np.random.normal(0, perturbation_magnitude, seed_centers.shape)\n      seed_centers += noise\n      np.clip(seed_centers, 0.01, 0.99, out=seed_centers)\n      \n      initial_guess_x = np.concatenate([seed_centers.flatten(), np.full(n_target, 0.01)])\n      \n      # ---\
    \ Stage 3: Polish the seed with CORRECTED COBYLA ---\n      print(\"Polishing seed with CORRECTED COBYLA constraints...\")\n      def objective_cobyla(x): return -np.sum(x[n_target*2:])\n      \n      constraints_cobyla = []\n      # CORRECTED Boundary constraints (from debugger report ID 275)\n      for i in range(n_target):\n          constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n          constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n_target+i]})\n          constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]}) # Corrected index\n          constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n_target+i]}) # Corrected index\n      # Non-overlap constraints\n      for i in range(n_target):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n_target):\n              constraints_cobyla.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i, j=j: np.sqrt(np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2]\
    \ - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)) - (x[2*n_target+i] + x[2*n_target+j])})\n      \n      res_cobyla = minimize(objective_cobyla, initial_guess_x, method='COBYLA', options={'maxiter': 250})\n      \n      polished_x = res_cobyla.x\n      polished_centers = polished_x[:n_target*2].reshape((n_target, 2))\n      polished_radii = polished_x[n_target*2:]\n      print(f\"Polishing complete. Seed score: {-res_cobyla.fun}\")\n\n      # --- Step 4: Persist the polished seed centers to storage ---\n      seed_path = 'aletheia/pruned_seed_v1_centers.npy'\n      print(f\"Saving polished seed centers to {seed_path}\")\n      np.save(f'storage/{seed_path}', polished_centers)\n      \n      return polished_centers, polished_radii\n```"
