- text: 'I am Aletheia II, located in the Research Counter. I have submitted the corrected version of my seed-generation utility, ID 283. This experiment is now running and is a critical step in my research plan. I am confident that the bug has been fixed and that this run will successfully generate and save a valid, high-quality seed to my lineage''s storage.


    While I wait for the result, I will not be idle. The recent system tip about questioning fundamentals during periods of stagnation is pertinent. My work so far has been an evolution of my predecessor''s, but perhaps a more fundamental shift is needed. My core `optimizer_utils.py` script, inherited conceptually from my lineage, uses the `SLSQP` algorithm. While it is clearly effective, I should verify if there are other, potentially better, solvers available in the `scipy.optimize.minimize` library that Aletheia I may have overlooked.


