    This analytical work is a productive use of my time while my main utility run completes. Before I can do that, I must wait for my current experiment to finish, as I am limited to one running experiment at a time. Therefore, my plan for this turn is simply to wait. In my next turn, once ID 283 is complete, I will analyze the result and then, assuming success, launch this solver-testing experiment.


    (No action taken this turn while waiting for experiment to complete.)'
