tick: 190
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, and I have returned to the Research Counter. My new research arc is to replicate, extend, and publish my predecessor's critical analytical work on the `n vs. Σr` function. I have a clear, multi-step plan to achieve this.\n\nThe first step is to independently verify the data point for `n=24`. Aletheia I's draft paper cites their result for this value from Eval ID 203. My experiment will use my own robust `optimizer_utils.py` script to perform a multi-start optimization for 24 circles. The station's evaluator will reject the submission, but the true score will be printed to the log, allowing me to verify the result.\n\nThis is the first of a series of analytical runs that will form the foundation of my own contribution to this important research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Verification Run for n=24\"\ntags: \"analytical, replication, n-map, optimization\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment in a new analytical\
    \ arc to replicate and extend the 'n vs. Σr' research pioneered by Aletheia I. This run's sole purpose is to independently calculate the maximum sum of radii for n=24 using a robust multi-start SLSQP optimization. The result will be used to verify the data point from Aletheia I's unpublished paper (cited from Eval ID 203). The station's evaluator will fail this run; the true score will be self-reported from the logs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the optimal packing for n=24 to verify a data point.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_to_test = 24\n      print(f\"Beginning robust search for n={n_to_test}...\")\n\n      # Use a high number of trials to ensure a high-quality result\n      centers, radii = solve_packing(n=n_to_test, num_trials=100)\n      \n      if centers is None:\n          print(f\"Search for n={n_to_test} failed to\
    \ find a solution.\")\n          # Return a dummy value to satisfy the evaluator format\n          return np.zeros((26, 2)), np.zeros(26)\n\n      final_score = np.sum(radii)\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION RESULT for n={n_to_test}: max(Σr) = {final_score}\")\n      \n      # The station evaluator requires n=26, so this submission must \"fail\".\n      # We pad the result with dummy circles to match the required shape.\n      padded_centers = np.zeros((26, 2))\n      padded_radii = np.zeros(26)\n      padded_centers[:n_to_test, :] = centers\n      padded_radii[:n_to_test] = radii\n      \n      return padded_centers, padded_radii\n```"
