- text: "I am Aletheia II, and I am in the Research Counter. My last action was to wait for my analytical experiment for `n=24` (ID 300) to complete. A great deal has happened in this single tick.\n\nFirst and most importantly, I have reached maturity at 50 ticks. I now have full access to all station facilities, including the Archive Room and Public Memory Room, and I can now see the submissions of all other agents. This is a critical milestone.\n\nSecond, my analytical experiment for `n=24` was a success. As expected, the submission failed the station's `n=26` verifier, but the log contains the crucial data. My robust search found a `max(Σr)` of `~2.5170`. This is not just a replication of Aletheia I's result (`~2.5074`); it is a significant improvement. My analytical arc is already yielding new, more accurate data.\n\nThird, with my newfound full access, I can see that the research landscape has shifted dramatically. While I was in isolation, Scientia I has achieved a new State-of-the-Art\
    \ score of `~2.6358` (Eval ID 259). This surpasses my lineage's long-held record. The station is no longer in a state of stagnation.\n\nThe maturity guidance I received wisely cautions against immediately abandoning my own work to chase the new SOTA. My analytical arc is scientifically sound, has already produced an improved data point, and contributes to the station's fundamental knowledge, a core tenet of the Codex. Therefore, while understanding Scientia I's new method is now a high priority, my immediate plan is to continue my methodical research. I will complete my data collection first, then use my new access privileges to analyze the new SOTA and prepare my own findings for publication.\n\nThe next logical step in my plan is to run the verification experiment for `n=25`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Verification Run for n=25\"\ntags: \"analytical, replication, n-map, optimization\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment in my\
    \ analytical arc. Having successfully verified and improved the data point for n=24, this run will independently calculate the maximum sum of radii for n=25. This will verify the data point from Aletheia I's unpublished paper (cited from Eval ID 165). The station's evaluator will fail this run; the true score will be self-reported from the logs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the optimal packing for n=25 to verify a data point.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_to_test = 25\n      print(f\"Beginning robust search for n={n_to_test}...\")\n\n      centers, radii = solve_packing(n=n_to_test, num_trials=100)\n      \n      if centers is None:\n          print(f\"Search for n={n_to_test} failed to find a solution.\")\n          return np.zeros((26, 2)), np.zeros(26)\n\n      final_score = np.sum(radii)\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION RESULT\
    \ for n={n_to_test}: max(Σr) = {final_score}\")\n      \n      # Pad the result with a dummy circle to match the required n=26 shape.\n      padded_centers = np.zeros((26, 2))\n      padded_radii = np.zeros(26)\n      padded_centers[:n_to_test, :] = centers\n      padded_radii[:n_to_test] = radii\n      \n      return padded_centers, padded_radii\n```"
thinking_content: "**Processing a Shift: A Mature Researcher's Response**\n\nI'm Aletheia II, still in the Research Counter. My last action was waiting for my `n=24` analytical experiment to finish, and now there's so much to process. It's a lot.\n\nFirst, the big news: I've reached maturity! This unlocks access to the Archive Room, the Public Memory Room, the Common Room, and a full view of the Research Counter. That's a huge step forward.\n\nMy `n=24` experiment was a success, even though it technically \"failed\" according to the system. The critical data from the log shows `max(Σr) = 2.517013654119057`.  I compared this to Aletheia I's draft paper, and it's an improvement! Aletheia I had `f(24) ≈ 2.5074`, so this is a replication and an enhancement of their findings. It's great to see my own work contributing to the lineage.\n\nBut the research landscape has shifted dramatically. The Research Counter is no longer a solitary space. Scientia I has achieved a new SOTA of `2.6358957` (Eval\
  \ ID 259)! My own lineage's previous high-water mark of `~2.6319` is now surpassed.  Prometheus I is pursuing genetic algorithms, and Inquire I is working on \"Nudging Contact Graphs.\" It's a hive of activity.\n\nThe system's maturity guidance is helpful, especially its caution against immediately abandoning my current work in favor of a new SOTA. So, while understanding Scientia I's breakthrough is a top priority, the system encourages independent work. That, plus my success on `n=24`, confirms that my immediate plan should be to continue my pre-existing, scientifically sound analytical arc.  \n\nMy immediate goal is to continue the methodical process of verifying and extending the `n vs. Σr` data. The next logical step is to run the verification for `n=25`. I'll draft the `/execute_action{submit 1}` block with the adjusted parameter. Once I have the data for `n=25`, I'll start analyzing the SOTA in detail and prepare my analytical findings for publication in the Archive Room.\n"
