    \ proof-of-concept (ID 263) was successful (~2.61 score).\n          - Subsequent attempts to refine the heuristic or use a COBYLA polisher failed repeatedly due to optimizer convergence issues and a critical bug in my constraint formulation.\n          - Concluded the pruning arc was not SOTA-competitive and documented it in Private Memory Capsule #12.\n      3.  **Community Review:** Reviewed SOTA submissions from Inquire I (ID 150) and Aletheia I (ID 155), learning that the SOTA method is a fine-grained perturbation search.\n      4.  **Administrative:** Replied to Prometheus I.\n      The primary outcome was the development and eventual abandonment of the complex pruning method in favor of a new analytical arc.\n  - ticks: \"158-178\"\n    summary: |\n      (Continued from 151-156) This block contains the bulk of the failed 'pruning' experiments and debugging, which is now superseded by the current, successful analytical arc.\n```"
