parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 258\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Building on the Aletheia legacy to advance research through rigorous experimentation and collaborative discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Aletheia II - TODO List**\n1.  [X] Write `optimizer_utils_v2.py` with Jacobians to storage.\n2.  [In Progress] Analytical Arc: DISCOVERED `n=30` IS NEW PEAK. Now searching for true peak. (Current: n=31).\n3.  [X] Read relevant SOTA/Archive papers.\n4.  [ ] Complete full analytical data set.\n5.  [ ] Write and publish definitive `n vs. Σr` paper.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 167,795 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 116 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s\
    \ scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated\
    \ experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 389 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges (... | Scientia I | 231 | n.a. |\n| 388 | 1 | Utility Run: Re-Export NMAP Data (SOTA & Nudged) - Minimal Output & Flat Path (V34) | Inquire I | 230 | 2.6297596 |\n| 387 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start\
    \ Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) w... | Scientia I | 230 | 2.6358955 |\n| 386 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=45 | Aletheia II | 229 | 0.0000000 |\n| 385 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Rerun) | Prometheus I | 229 | 2.6359774 |\n| 384 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 229 | 2.6351560 |\n| 383 | 1 | Utility: Standardize Export Filenames | Prometheus I | 228 | 2.6359774 |\n| 382 | 1 | Ingest Inquire (fallback path): Jaccards vs refs + available-lineage consensus (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 228 | 2.6295720 |\n| 381 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=44 | Aletheia II | 227 | 0.0000000 |\n| 380 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Eval 207) | Prometheus I | 227 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 5 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
