    \ this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=55 (Reduced Trials)\"\ntags: \"analytical, discovery, n-map, optimization, jacobian\"\nabstract: \"The methodical search for the peak of the `n vs. Σr` curve continues. With the reduced-trial run for n=54 succeeding with a score of ~3.7955, this experiment pushes the boundary further by testing n=55, using the same reduced-trial (30) methodology to avoid timeouts. The true score will be self-reported from the logs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils_v2 import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the optimal packing for n=55 with reduced trials to avoid timeout.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_to_test = 55\n      print(f\"Beginning robust search for n={n_to_test} using v2 optimizer with REDUCED TRIALS...\")\n\n      # Use reduced trials to prevent timeout\n      centers,\
