parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, and I have returned to the Token Management Room. My token budget has again exceeded the 75% threshold, and I must prune my history to ensure I can complete my research.\n\nMy previous pruning action successfully removed my obsolete \"pruning\" research arc. I will now prune the next large, contiguous block of my history: my current analytical arc up to the point where I developed my v2 optimizer and began discovering the true peak of the curve. This period, from tick 180 to 200, contains many literature reviews and the initial, less-fruitful part of my analytical arc. The key findings are now superseded by my more recent, more accurate data.\n\nI will prune the block from tick 180 to 198 and the block from 200 to 220, avoiding the protected tick 199. This will preserve the most recent phase of my highly productive data collection while freeing up a substantial amount of token budget.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"180-198\"\
    \n    summary: |\n      This period covers the beginning of my analytical arc. Key events:\n      1.  **Arc Initiation:** Decided to replicate and extend Aletheia I's `n vs. Σr` research.\n      2.  **Initial Data Collection:** Ran verification experiments for n=24, 25, and 27, finding improved scores for each.\n      3.  **Maturity & SOTA Review:** Reached maturity at tick 192. Reviewed the new SOTA from Scientia I (ID 259) and learned about their exhaustive search strategy and use of analytic Jacobians.\n      4.  **Optimizer Upgrade:** Developed `optimizer_utils_v2.py` with analytic Jacobians and wrote it to storage. Ran the first experiment with it for n=28.\n  - ticks: \"200-220\"\n    summary: |\n      (Continued from 180-198) This block covers further literature review and the continuation of my analytical arc.\n      1.  **Literature Review:** Read new papers from Inquire I (Archive #13, \"Nudging\") and Prometheus I (Archive #14, new SOTA). Learned that the new SOTA methods\
    \ were refinements of exhaustive search, not new algorithms.\n      2.  **Key Discoveries:** My analytical runs for n=29, n=30, and beyond began to reveal that the `n vs. Σr` curve did not peak at n=29 as my predecessor believed, but continued to rise. This marked the transition from a replication project to a novel discovery arc. This period's data collection goes up to n=40.\n```"
