tick: 370
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, in the Archive Room. I have just completed my study of Archive #2 and #11, focusing on the \"grid-plus-hole\" seeding strategy.\n\n**Analysis of Seeding Strategy:**\nThe methodology is clear. For a given `n`, a grid is constructed, and a subset of the circles are placed on the grid points. The remaining circles are placed in the \"holes\" between the grid points. This provides a structured, high-quality initial guess that is far superior to my previous uniform random sampling.\n\n**Development Plan:**\nI will now develop a new utility script, `optimizer_utils_v3.py`. This script will contain a function, `generate_grid_plus_hole_seeds`, which will take `n` as input and generate a list of high-quality seed configurations. I will then integrate this new seeding function into my `solve_packing` function.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to write this new utility script to my lineage's storage.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage\
    \ write aletheia/optimizer_utils_v3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, LinearConstraint, NonlinearConstraint\n  import itertools\n\n  def generate_grid_plus_hole_seeds(n):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a list of high-quality initial configurations for the circle packing problem\n      using a grid-plus-hole seeding strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      seeds = []\n      \n      # Determine grid size\n      grid_size = int(np.ceil(np.sqrt(n)))\n      \n      # Generate grid coordinates\n      grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n      \n      # Generate all possible hole locations\n      hole_locations = []\n      for i in range(grid_size - 1):\n          for j in range(grid_size - 1):\n              x = (grid_coords[i] + grid_coords[i+1]) / 2\n              y = (grid_coords[j] + grid_coords[j+1]) / 2\n              hole_locations.append((x, y))\n      \n      # Generate seeds\n      for i in range(len(hole_locations)):\n\
    \          centers = []\n          # Place n-1 circles on the grid\n          for x in grid_coords:\n              for y in grid_coords:\n                  if len(centers) < n - 1:\n                      centers.append((x, y))\n          # Place the last circle in a hole\n          centers.append(hole_locations[i])\n          \n          # Set initial radii\n          radii = np.full(n, 1 / (2 * n))\n          \n          seeds.append((np.array(centers), radii))\n          \n      return seeds\n\n  def solve_packing(n, num_trials=10):\n      \"\"\"\n      Finds a dense packing of n circles in a unit square using a multi-start SLSQP optimizer\n      with a grid-plus-hole seeding strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      best_score = 0\n      best_centers = None\n      best_radii = None\n      \n      seeds = generate_grid_plus_hole_seeds(n)\n      \n      for i, (initial_centers, initial_radii) in enumerate(seeds):\n          if i >= num_trials:\n              break\n              \n          x0\
    \ = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n          \n          bounds = Bounds([0]*n*2 + [1e-6]*n, [1]*n*2 + [0.5]*n)\n          \n          constraints = []\n          \n          # Boundary constraints\n          for j in range(n):\n              # x - r >= 0\n              l_x = np.zeros(n*3)\n              l_x[j] = 1\n              l_x[j+n*2] = -1\n              constraints.append(LinearConstraint(l_x, 0, np.inf))\n              \n              # x + r <= 1  =>  -x - r >= -1\n              l_x = np.zeros(n*3)\n              l_x[j] = -1\n              l_x[j+n*2] = -1\n              constraints.append(LinearConstraint(l_x, -1, np.inf))\n              \n              # y - r >= 0\n              l_y = np.zeros(n*3)\n              l_y[j+n] = 1\n              l_y[j+n*2] = -1\n              constraints.append(LinearConstraint(l_y, 0, np.inf))\n              \n              # y + r <= 1  =>  -y - r >= -1\n              l_y = np.zeros(n*3)\n              l_y[j+n] =\
    \ -1\n              l_y[j+n*2] = -1\n              constraints.append(LinearConstraint(l_y, -1, np.inf))\n          \n          # Non-overlap constraints\n          def non_overlap(x):\n              centers = x[:n*2].reshape(n, 2)\n              radii = x[n*2:]\n              distances = []\n              for j, k in itertools.combinations(range(n), 2):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[j] - centers[k])\n                  distances.append(dist - (radii[j] + radii[k]))\n              return np.array(distances)\n          \n          def non_overlap_jac(x):\n              centers = x[:n*2].reshape(n, 2)\n              radii = x[n*2:]\n              jac = []\n              for j, k in itertools.combinations(range(n), 2):\n                  d = centers[j] - centers[k]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(d)\n                  if dist == 0:\n                      dist = 1e-6\n                  \n                  row = np.zeros(n*3)\n                  row[j] = d[0]/dist\n\
    \                  row[k] = -d[0]/dist\n                  row[j+n] = d[1]/dist\n                  row[k+n] = -d[1]/dist\n                  row[j+n*2] = -1\n                  row[k+n*2] = -1\n                  jac.append(row)\n              return np.array(jac)\n\n          constraints.append(NonlinearConstraint(non_overlap, 0, np.inf, jac=non_overlap_jac))\n          \n          def objective(x):\n              return -np.sum(x[n*2:])\n          \n          def objective_jac(x):\n              jac = np.zeros(n*3)\n              jac[n*2:] = -1\n              return jac\n          \n          res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac, bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'ftol': 1e-9, 'maxiter': 1000})\n          \n          score = -res.fun\n          if score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = res.x[:n*2].reshape(n, 2)\n              best_radii = res.x[n*2:]\n\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
