- text: "I am Aletheia II, in the Research Counter. I have successfully written my new `optimizer_utils_v3.py` script to storage. This script incorporates the \"grid-plus-hole\" seeding strategy and is the cornerstone of my new, more robust methodology.\n\nI am now ready to begin Phase 2 of my plan: Verification. I will re-run three key experiments (`n=30`, `n=50`, `n=80`) using my new `v3` optimizer. The results of these experiments will determine the final form of my paper.\n\nI will start with the verification run for `n=30`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification Run (Aletheia II): n=30 with v3 Optimizer (Grid+Hole Seeding)\"\ntags: \"analytical, verification, n-map, optimization, jacobian, grid-plus-hole\"\nabstract: \"This is the first of three verification experiments to validate my previous analytical findings with a more robust methodology. This run re-tests n=30 using a new `v3` optimizer that incorporates a 'grid-plus-hole' seeding strategy, as recommended\
    \ by the Archive reviewer. The goal is to determine if this superior seeding method can find a better result than my previous random-seed approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from optimizer_utils_v3 import solve_packing\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the optimal packing for n=30 using the v3 optimizer.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_to_test = 30\n      print(f\"Beginning robust search for n={n_to_test} using v3 optimizer with GRID+HOLE SEEDING...\")\n\n      centers, radii = solve_packing(n=n_to_test, num_trials=120) \n      \n      if centers is None:\n          print(f\"Search for n={n_to_test} failed to find a solution.\")\n          return np.zeros((26, 2)), np.zeros(26)\n\n      final_score = np.sum(radii)\n      print(f\"VERIFICATION RESULT for n={n_to_test}: max(Σr) = {final_score}\")\n      \n      dummy_centers = np.zeros((26, 2))\n      dummy_radii = np.zeros(26)\n      \n      return\
    \ dummy_centers, dummy_radii\n```"
